  "scope": "A formation is classified by its relation to the conditions of the relations it participates in (dependence or drawing): renewing when each such condition keeps supporting every formation depending on it, consuming when it draws on a condition some dependent formation permanently loses. Exclusive, not exhaustive. Unrenewed drawdown admits finitely many active steps. In a law where the renewing formation depends on the condition it renews: within renewal, continuation and unbounded formation; beyond renewal, permanent loss of the renewer's support, self-ending with bounded formation for a dependent focal formation, and unbounded persistence for an independent one. Neither formation at each active step nor the focal formation's own trajectory decides the class; joint drawing can consume when each alone is within renewal; escalation beginning within renewal consumes. No ethical predicate; every declaration is required to have an empty axiom set. Levels, needs and rates are local representations whose real correspondence is not established. RenewalComparison connects this to GenerativeComparison's G0 and C as hypotheses only: under the relational reading (active events of non-consuming formations as grounds), G0 credits exactly non-consuming formation events, and for every law of the family drawing beyond renewal C ranks the unfolding with the focal formation below the same unfolding without it, which the broad event reading leaves incomparable and lets an irreflexive, transitive C-respecting comparison invert; sharing extends winning by consumption under both readings. The comparisons use C, not G0; the relational reading of G0's generation and C's defense are philosophical, outside this audit; mixed cases are not decided.",
  "lean_binary_sha256": "b48bc5ab229bd8b320a224b87e20fc428dba6fa8a1c054bd4fa6def846e19997",
